      "fact": "Special Master Judge Pierre N. Leval issued a 100-page report in May 2021 regarding the escheatment of MoneyGram checks.",
      "source_date": "2021-05-20"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "fact": "The Special Master's May 2021 report concluded that disputed MoneyGram 'official checks' should be returned to the states of original purchase under the Federal Disposition of Abandoned Money Orders and Traveler's Checks Act.",
      "source_date": "2021-05-20"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "fact": "The Special Master found Delaware's argument that the checks did not fall under the FDA classification to be 'flawed,' 'insubstantial,' and 'unpersuasive.'",
