      "fact": "Delaware's legal position in the case was that MoneyGram's 'official checks' are not 'similar written instruments' under the FDA.",
      "source_date": "2022-01-10"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "fact": "Thirty intervening states argued that MoneyGram official checks are functionally equivalent to money orders and should escheat to the place of purchase.",
      "source_date": "2022-01-10"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "fact": "The Federal Disposition of Abandoned Money Orders and Traveler's Checks Act (FDA) mandates that money orders, traveler's checks, and 'other similar written instruments' escheat to the state where the instrument was purchased.",
