      "fact": "In House v. Bell (2006), the Supreme Court clarified that the 'actual innocence' gateway requires a showing that, in light of new evidence, it is more likely than not that no reasonable juror would have convicted the petitioner.",
      "source_date": "2006-06-21"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "fact": "The Supreme Court decided Teague v. Lane, 489 U.S. 288 in 1989.",
      "source_date": "1989-03-22"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "fact": "In Teague v. Lane (1989), the Supreme Court held that new rules of constitutional law generally do not apply retroactively to cases on collateral review.",
      "source_date": "1989-03-22"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "fact": "The Supreme Court decided Gray v. Netherland, 518 U.S. 152 in 1996.",
      "source_date": "1996-05-28"
