      "fact": "In Gray v. Netherland (1996), the Supreme Court held that a claim requiring the adoption of a new constitutional rule is procedurally barred on federal habeas review if the petitioner failed to raise it in state court, unless cause and prejudice are shown.",
      "source_date": "1996-05-28"
